        "date": "2026-11-26T11:54:34Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): the cycle 200/205 level needs the complete NC identifier\n\nThe #4172 review found that drillLevel() matched a prefix of the NC\nsoftware string and accepted release zero and unsupported variants.\nOne guard now parses the complete canonical identifier (6 digits, \"-\",\n2 release digits, optional \" SP<n>\"). A table row must then match the\nmodel, the family, the variant range and a release that the research\nnames. Anything else with a stated identity is refused by name.\n\nFixes #4094\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
